<div class="page-header">
  <h1 class="page-title">The project</h1>
</div>

<div class="page-prose">
  <p class="page-lead">
    Lugares Míticos de Jaén was a non-profit project that collected and showed to the world the
    heritage of the province of Jaén, in southern Spain. Its main purpose was to make that
    heritage known, and to help us, the people from Jaén, learn to appreciate it, enjoy it and
    protect it properly.
  </p>

  <p>
    Between <strong>3 June 2013</strong> and <strong>17 December 2018</strong> we published
    <strong>164 articles</strong> across <strong>97 towns and villages</strong> of the province,
    and two books. This site preserves that archive in full.
  </p>

  <p>
    There was no announcement and no goodbye: publishing simply grew further apart until it
    stopped. What follows is the story of what we did while it lasted.
  </p>
</div>

<section class="page-section">
  <h2 class="page-section--title">The story</h2>

  <ol class="timeline">
    <li class="timeline--item timeline--item__last">
      <p class="timeline--date">26 October 2026</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">A new site for the archive</h3>
      <p>
        We rebuilt the site as a static one, lighter and easier to keep, so that the archive stays
        up now that we no longer publish. Every old page is still at its old address, and there is
        plenty that is new:
      </p>
      <ul class="page-list">
        <li>All 164 articles in English: the 107 that were missing, translated automatically.</li>
        <li>A search on the home page, which finds places, towns and the text of the articles.</li>
        <li>The province's ten regions, each with its articles and municipalities.</li>
        <li>The map of the whole province, filtered by municipality and category, now with the traditional crafts.</li>
        <li>Other articles nearby at the end of each one, and a home page that changes every day.</li>
        <li>The language switch takes you to the same page in the other language.</li>
        <li>Photos that load as you reach them, so everything is faster.</li>
        <li>And many small improvements to make the site easier to browse, on a phone too.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">17 December 2018</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">The last article</h3>
      <p>
        We published <a href="/en/articles/yacimiento-del-giribaile">the Giribaile site</a>, in
        Vilches. It was article number 164 and, without our knowing it at the time, the last one.
        That year we had published twelve, against the forty-three of 2014.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">5 December 2017</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">The second book</h3>
      <p>
        We presented the second book of Lugares Míticos de Jaén, again at the Old Hospital San
        Juan de Dios in Jaén. Sixteen more chapters, opened by a piece from
        <strong>Antonio Muñoz Molina</strong>, "Jaén, cerca y lejos".
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">24 October 2017</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">A second crowdfunding campaign</h3>
      <p>
        We went back to Verkami to fund the second book. We asked for a minimum of €4,500 and
        gathered around <strong>€5,500</strong>.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">10 October 2016</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">Traditional crafts</h3>
      <p>
        Until then we had told the story of places. With
        <a href="/en/articles/el-mimbre">Wickerwork</a> we started a different format, about the
        crafts still practised in the province. They took far more work, so we only managed three:
        that one was followed by <a href="/en/articles/la-forja">Ironwork</a> and
        <a href="/en/articles/la-zapateria">The shoemaker's</a>.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">9 November 2015</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">100 articles</h3>
      <p>
        We published our hundredth article, dedicated to the
        <a href="/en/articles/puente-de-ariza">Puente de Ariza</a>, in Úbeda. We shipped several
        improvements alongside it: a redesigned navigation menu, a slider with the latest articles
        on the homepage, and a map with directions on how to reach each place.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">September 2015</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">The new website</h3>
      <img class="timeline--image" src="{% static_image '/files/about/web-v3.png' %}" width="1552" height="985" alt="The Lugares Míticos de Jaén website in 2015" loading="lazy">
      <p>
        We significantly improved the maps and added a page for every town and village, so you
        could comfortably discover Jaén from your sofa. We also reworked the design of the article
        pages and put real effort into the mobile experience. And, importantly, from that point on
        the site was available in English too.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">June 2015</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">The first book</h3>
      <img class="timeline--image" src="{% static_image '/files/about/foto-presentacion.jpg' %}" width="914" height="553" alt="The first book being presented at the Old Hospital San Juan de Dios" loading="lazy">
      <p>
        After months of hard work, on 25 June we presented the first book of Lugares Míticos de
        Jaén and celebrated the project's second anniversary with more than 200 people at the Old
        Hospital San Juan de Dios, alongside the sixteen authors who joined us on the adventure.
      </p>
      <img class="timeline--image" src="{% static_image '/files/about/foto-libros-imprenta.jpg' %}" width="900" height="600" alt="The first printed copies of the book" loading="lazy">
      <p>Weeks earlier we had received the first printed copies.</p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">7 February 2015</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">€6,000 raised</h3>
      <img class="timeline--image" src="{% static_image '/files/about/crowdfundeado.jpg' %}" width="200" height="200" alt="The crowdfunding campaign, funded" loading="lazy">
      <p>
        It was hard, but we made it. After 40 days of madness the campaign closed at almost
        <strong>€6,000</strong>, well above the original goal. That paid for a first print run of
        600 copies while we kept up our usual publishing pace.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">December 2014</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">We launch a crowdfunding campaign</h3>
      <p>
        We needed funding to keep the website going. Many people had asked us "why don't you
        publish a book?", so we started a campaign on Verkami to raise what we needed to publish
        the first book of Lugares Míticos de Jaén.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">June 2014</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">Our first birthday</h3>
      <img class="timeline--image" src="{% static_image '/files/about/castillo.jpg' %}" width="150" height="150" alt="Santa Catalina Castle" loading="lazy">
      <p>
        To celebrate it we published a special series of articles about Santa Catalina Castle and
        raffled three full-colour printed pictures.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">September 2013</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">The first redesign</h3>
      <p>
        The archive of places kept growing, people wanted to know more about the project and sent
        us plenty of suggestions. To improve the experience we added a map with every article
        geolocated, along with a homepage collecting the most recent and most visited articles.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="timeline--item">
      <p class="timeline--date">3 June 2013</p>
      <h3 class="timeline--title">The first article</h3>
      <img class="timeline--image" src="{% static_image '/files/about/primer-logotipo.png' %}" width="150" height="150" alt="The first Lugares Míticos de Jaén logo" loading="lazy">
      <p>
        The initial idea was simple: publish a weekly article about one of the many charming places
        in our province, visually striking and with short texts — something you could read in two
        minutes and that left you wanting to know more. The first one was
        <a href="/en/articles/el-posito">El Pósito</a>.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

